{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('update.json'))\n\nd['rationale']=(\\\"Interpreted the completed probe receipt for @verify_quorum (all three comparisons holds, 6 parsed events, 0 parsing errors) and opened a second question on the authority-transition axis: LeadershipTransferToServer accepts a non-voter as its target. The source trace shows the leader looks the target up in leaderState.replState, which startStopReplication populates for non-voters too, so TimeoutNow reaches a server that cannot win an election, while its campaign still forces every voter to adopt the higher term and reject it. A two-case probe (voter target as control, non-voter target) records what the call reports against which server actually takes leadership; its execution is requested. The registered gap about the stale-read overlap condition is answered with the partial progress from the receipt and stays open.\\\")\n\nd['sources'] += [\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":2232,\\\"end_line\\\":2237,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":296,\\\"end_line\\\":303,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1684,\\\"end_line\\\":1706,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":760,\\\"end_line\\\":790,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":735,\\\"end_line\\\":758,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"pick_server_voters\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":2186,\\\"end_line\\\":2208,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1290,\\\"end_line\\\":1330,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"docs_transfer\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"docs/README.md\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":48,\\\"end_line\\\":48,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n]\n\nd['investigations'].append({\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@transfer_nonvoter\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"When LeadershipTransferToServer names a non-voter, does the call report a transfer that the named server can actually complete, and what happens to the cluster's leadership while it cannot?\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"pick_server_voters\\\",\\\"docs_transfer\\\"],\n \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"The leader does not check that the requested target holds a vote. It resolves the target through leaderState.replState, which holds an entry for every configured server except the leader itself, so a non-voter passes that check and receives TimeoutNow; timeoutNow makes it a candidate with candidateFromLeadershipTransfer set, which skips pre-vote by design, so it sends a real RequestVote with a higher term. Each voter adopts that higher term and steps down before reaching the hasVote rejection, then refuses the vote because the candidate has no vote, so no server grants the transfer, yet the leader's transfer goroutine reports success when it observes its own leadership loss. The prediction is that the call returns nil while the requested target never becomes leader, whereas the same call naming a voter does transfer leadership.\\\",\n \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"The transfer future's reported result compared with the state of the requested target and of the cluster's leadership, in two cases that differ only in the target's suffrage in the leader's latest configuration.\\\"\n})\n\nd['knowledge'].append({\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@transfer_accepts_nonvoter\\\",\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"LeadershipTransferToServer accepts a non-voter target and reports success without transferring leadership to it. The leader resolves the requested ID in leaderState.replState, which contains an entry for every configured server except the leader (startStopReplication creates one per server without consulting Suffrage) and only errors with 'cannot find replication state' when no entry exists. The selected target is sent TimeoutNow, which sets it to Candidate and marks candidateFromLeadershipTransfer; that flag makes runCandidate skip pre-vote, so the target sends a real RequestVote carrying the next term. A voter handling that request adopts the higher term and becomes a follower before it reaches the hasVote check, which then refuses the vote because the candidate holds no vote; the candidate therefore cannot win. When the old leader observes the higher term it steps down, the transfer goroutine's leftLeaderLoop branch responds nil, and the caller sees success. By contrast LeadershipTransfer with no explicit target picks through pickServer, which skips every server whose Suffrage is not Voter.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Protocol version >= 3 (otherwise LeadershipTransferToServer returns ErrUnsupportedProtocol), a cluster whose latest configuration at the leader contains the named server with Suffrage other than Voter, and pre-vote enabled or disabled (the transfer path skips pre-vote either way). The named server must be reachable from the leader, otherwise the leader reports a TimeoutNow failure instead.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"start_stop_repl\\\",\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"pick_server_voters\\\",\\\"follower_vote_grant\\\",\\\"docs_transfer\\\"]\n})\n\nd['gaps'].append({\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@transfer_nonvoter\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"After a transfer request naming a non-voter, how long is the cluster without a leader, and does the previous leader lose leadership and the higher term before a new election completes?\\\"\n})\n\nd['interpretations']=[\n {\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@verify_quorum\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"verify_leader\\\",\\\"quorum_size\\\",\\\"start_stop_repl\\\",\\\"notify_all\\\",\\\"verify_vote\\\",\\\"update_last_appended\\\",\\\"heartbeat_ack\\\",\\\"api_verify_leader\\\",\\\"lease_check\\\",\\\"config_validation\\\",\\\"reload_config\\\"],\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"VerifyLeader's documented role is to ensure this peer is still the leader so that stale data is not returned from the FSM. The question was whether its success establishes voter-majority contact; the execution says it does not. In the retained run of the three-partition probe, the leader whose only reachable peer was the non-voter returned success in 0ms while its own latest configuration reported three voters, one non-voter and a quorum size of 2, and the leader was still in Leader state (parsed event index 1); the control partition that kept one voter reachable also returned success, which shows the harness does observe a genuine acknowledgement path (index 3); the control partition with no reachable peer did not return success at all, returning 'leadership lost while committing log' after 202ms with the node in Follower state, so the leader cannot reach the threshold on its own vote and the non-voter acknowledgement is what satisfied it in the first case (index 5). All three declared comparisons hold with the setup event matched as admission (correlations 1->0, 3->2, 5->4). The source explains the mechanism: verifyLeader asks every entry of leaderState.replState to acknowledge, startStopReplication creates such an entry for every configured server except the leader without consulting Suffrage, any successful AppendEntries or InstallSnapshot reply from such a peer calls notifyAll(true) and increments verifyFuture.votes, and the threshold compared against is quorumSize(), counted over voters alone. The same package treats voter eligibility strictly in its other leadership tests: checkLeaderLease does not count a non-voter, requestVote refuses a candidate that holds no vote, and quorumSize itself counts only voters, so the verify path is the outlier rather than a deliberate relaxation. \\\"\n   \\\"The consequence for reads stays bounded and is not what this receipt measures. The leader's lease is voter-only, and both Config.Validate and ReloadConfig enforce LeaderLeaseTimeout <= HeartbeatTimeout <= ElectionTimeout, so the old leader is normally removed before a voter majority elects a successor; the no-peer control is exactly that lease firing at 202ms with a 200ms lease. What the receipt does establish is the weaker but unconditional part: for an interval in which the leader exchanged nothing with any other voter, VerifyLeader reports success, so a caller relying on that call for read consistency is really relying on the lease timer rather than on the acknowledgements VerifyLeader collected.\\\"),\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"checkLeaderLease counts voters only, so a leader that has lost voter-majority contact steps down within about LeaderLeaseTimeout; the no-peer control shows this concretely (leadership lost at 202ms with a 200ms lease), which bounds the stale-read consequence rather than showing the verify decision support to be adequate.\\\",\n   \\\"Config.Validate keeps LeaderLeaseTimeout <= HeartbeatTimeout <= ElectionTimeout, and ReloadConfig re-runs ValidateConfig, so a leader cannot be configured to outlive a follower's election timer through the public reload API.\\\",\n   \\\"In the non-voter partition the other servers stayed in term 2 with no leader change, so the receipt does not witness a successor being elected while the old leader still verified; that half of the consequence remains unobserved.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The stale-read consequence still needs a successor elected while the old leader reports verify success, for example a leader-side stall or clock jump longer than ElectionTimeout - LeaderLeaseTimeout, or a verify request served before a ready lease case; the registered gap tracks that search and is not resolved by this receipt.\\\",\n   \\\"The probe uses one process with real Raft instances and in-memory transports, so it exercises the leader's own replication and verify paths but not process-level partitions or multi-host clocks; the partition was made by disconnecting transports in both directions.\\\",\n   \\\"One execution of each case is cited; repeatability of the timing-sensitive control (the 202ms lease step-down) is not established.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"b02d5ff23a504a8ea38116085ba8e23c\\\":[0,1,2,3,4,5]}\n },\n {\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@transfer_nonvoter\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"pick_server_voters\\\",\\\"follower_vote_grant\\\",\\\"docs_transfer\\\",\\\"start_stop_repl\\\"],\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"conditional\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"The documented purpose of LeadershipTransferToServer is to transition leadership to a specific server in the cluster, and the only target validation in the leader is a lookup in leaderState.replState, which holds an entry for every configured server except the leader regardless of Suffrage; a missing entry is the sole error. A non-voter therefore passes validation and is sent TimeoutNow, which makes it a Candidate with candidateFromLeadershipTransfer set, a flag that by design suppresses pre-vote so the node sends a real RequestVote with a higher term. Voters processing that request adopt the higher term and set themselves to Follower before the hasVote check rejects the candidate, so the candidate cannot collect a single grant, while the old leader loses leadership because it adopts the higher term too and its transfer goroutine then reports success from the leftLeaderLoop branch. The account is asserted on that source basis and stays conditional until the requested two-case probe reports what the call returns versus which server actually takes leadership; the controlling contrast is the same call naming a voter, and the note that auto-targeted LeadershipTransfer() skips non-voters via pickServer shows the library itself does not consider a non-voter a valid transfer target when it chooses.\\\"),\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The API does not state in its comment that the target must be a voter, and a caller who names only voters never reaches this path, so the defect depends on an accepted calling pattern rather than on the library's own choice of target.\\\",\n   \\\"LeadershipTransfer() without an explicit target filters non-voters in pickServer, which shows the intended transfer target set is the voter set and supports reading the targeted call as requiring the same premise.\\\",\n   \\\"A TimeoutNow that cannot be delivered (unreachable target) is reported as an error by the transfer path, so not every unusable target is silently accepted.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"No receipt exists yet for this question; the harness for the two-case probe is submitted with this update and its outcome is predicted, not observed.\\\",\n   \\\"Whether the cluster is briefly leaderless after the non-voter's campaign, and for how long, is registered as a gap: the current probe samples leadership state at the end of a 1500ms window, which is too coarse to bound a leaderless interval.\\\",\n   \\\"The claim concerns the reported result of the call and the requested target's inability to win; it does not assert data loss, since committed entries remain committed and a fresh election follows.\\\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@transfer_nonvoter\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"pick_server_voters\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Observe what LeadershipTransferToServer reports against which server actually takes leadership when the requested target is a non-voter, with the same call naming a voter as the only difference. Each case emits an assurance_transfer_target setup event describing the leader, the chosen target, its suffrage in the leader's latest configuration and the voter set, then an assurance_transfer_result event with the returned result, the target's and old leader's states, the leader set and terms after the call, and the time until any leader is observed.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n   \\\"Three voters plus one non-voter is a supported configuration; the non-voter is joined through the leader's own AddNonvoter call.\\\",\n   \\\"HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 200ms and CommitTimeout = 5ms satisfy Config.Validate; protocol version is the default (>= 3), so LeadershipTransferToServer is supported.\\\",\n   \\\"A voter target is a legal and expected use, so the voter case is the control that the probe can observe a real transfer rather than a probe that never succeeds.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\n   \\\"Bounding the length of any leaderless interval: leadership state is sampled at the end of the 1500ms observation window, so this probe does not measure an interval.\\\"\n  ]\n },\n \\\"prefix\\\":(\\\"Each case builds four real Raft instances in one process, each with its own InmemStore, InmemSnapshotStore and InmemTransport, fully connected before any node starts. Three voters are bootstrapped with BootstrapCluster from a configuration naming them as Voter; the fourth node is started without a configuration and joined through the elected leader's own AddNonvoter(id, address, 0, 5s) call, waiting until the leader's latest configuration reports it. \\\"\n  \\\"The target is then chosen by configuration role, never by a measured result: in the control case the first voter that is not the leader, in the probe case the joined non-voter; its suffrage is read back from the leader's latest configuration and reported in the setup event. The case calls leader.LeadershipTransferToServer(target.id, target.addr), waits up to 5s for the returned result, then waits up to 1500ms for the requested target to be observed as Leader and separately for any node to be Leader, and finally records the leader set, the maximum term across all four nodes and whether that term rose above the leader's term before the call. Both cases share the harness TestAssuranceLeadershipTransferTarget and are emitted under distinct case names.\\\"),\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_target\\\"}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"transfer_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"nil\\\"},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: what the call reported. Holds means the predicted success report was observed, which supports the defect account rather than contradicting it.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_became_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: the requested server never became leader within the observation window.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_became_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Voter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Voter target control: the same call does transfer leadership, so the non-voter outcome is not a probe that never transfers.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"transfer_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"nil\\\"},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Voter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Voter target control: the reported result for a transfer that does complete.\\\"}\n ]\n}\n\njson.dump(d, open('update.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nopen('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -6\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('update.json'))\n\nd['rationale']=(\\\"Interpreted the completed probe receipt for @verify_quorum (all three comparisons holds, 6 parsed events, 0 parsing errors) and opened a second question on the authority-transition axis: LeadershipTransferToServer accepts a non-voter as its target. The source trace shows the leader looks the target up in leaderState.replState, which startStopReplication populates for non-voters too, so TimeoutNow reaches a server that cannot win an election, while its campaign still forces every voter to adopt the higher term and reject it. A two-case probe (voter target as control, non-voter target) records what the call reports against which server actually takes leadership; its execution is requested. The registered gap about the stale-read overlap condition is answered with the partial progress from the receipt and stays open.\\\")\n\nd['sources'] += [\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":2232,\\\"end_line\\\":2237,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":296,\\\"end_line\\\":303,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1684,\\\"end_line\\\":1706,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":760,\\\"end_line\\\":790,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":735,\\\"end_line\\\":758,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"pick_server_voters\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":2186,\\\"end_line\\\":2208,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1290,\\\"end_line\\\":1330,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"docs_transfer\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"docs/README.md\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":48,\\\"end_line\\\":48,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n]\n\nd['investigations'].append({\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@transfer_nonvoter\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"When LeadershipTransferToServer names a non-voter, does the call report a transfer that the named server can actually complete, and what happens to the cluster's leadership while it cannot?\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"pick_server_voters\\\",\\\"docs_transfer\\\"],\n \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"The leader does not check that the requested target holds a vote. It resolves the target through leaderState.replState, which holds an entry for every configured server except the leader itself, so a non-voter passes that check and receives TimeoutNow; timeoutNow makes it a candidate with candidateFromLeadershipTransfer set, which skips pre-vote by design, so it sends a real RequestVote with a higher term. Each voter adopts that higher term and steps down before reaching the hasVote rejection, then refuses the vote because the candidate has no vote, so no server grants the transfer, yet the leader's transfer goroutine reports success when it observes its own leadership loss. The prediction is that the call returns nil while the requested target never becomes leader, whereas the same call naming a voter does transfer leadership.\\\",\n \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"The transfer future's reported result compared with the state of the requested target and of the cluster's leadership, in two cases that differ only in the target's suffrage in the leader's latest configuration.\\\"\n})\n\nd['knowledge'].append({\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@transfer_accepts_nonvoter\\\",\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"LeadershipTransferToServer accepts a non-voter target and reports success without transferring leadership to it. The leader resolves the requested ID in leaderState.replState, which contains an entry for every configured server except the leader (startStopReplication creates one per server without consulting Suffrage) and only errors with 'cannot find replication state' when no entry exists. The selected target is sent TimeoutNow, which sets it to Candidate and marks candidateFromLeadershipTransfer; that flag makes runCandidate skip pre-vote, so the target sends a real RequestVote carrying the next term. A voter handling that request adopts the higher term and becomes a follower before it reaches the hasVote check, which then refuses the vote because the candidate holds no vote; the candidate therefore cannot win. When the old leader observes the higher term it steps down, the transfer goroutine's leftLeaderLoop branch responds nil, and the caller sees success. By contrast LeadershipTransfer with no explicit target picks through pickServer, which skips every server whose Suffrage is not Voter.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Protocol version >= 3 (otherwise LeadershipTransferToServer returns ErrUnsupportedProtocol), a cluster whose latest configuration at the leader contains the named server with Suffrage other than Voter, and pre-vote enabled or disabled (the transfer path skips pre-vote either way). The named server must be reachable from the leader, otherwise the leader reports a TimeoutNow failure instead.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"start_stop_repl\\\",\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"pick_server_voters\\\",\\\"follower_vote_grant\\\",\\\"docs_transfer\\\"]\n})\n\nd['gaps'].append({\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@transfer_nonvoter\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"After a transfer request naming a non-voter, how long is the cluster without a leader, and does the previous leader lose leadership and the higher term before a new election completes?\\\"\n})\n\nd['interpretations']=[\n {\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@verify_quorum\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"verify_leader\\\",\\\"quorum_size\\\",\\\"start_stop_repl\\\",\\\"notify_all\\\",\\\"verify_vote\\\",\\\"update_last_appended\\\",\\\"heartbeat_ack\\\",\\\"api_verify_leader\\\",\\\"lease_check\\\",\\\"config_validation\\\",\\\"reload_config\\\"],\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"VerifyLeader's documented role is to ensure this peer is still the leader so that stale data is not returned from the FSM. The question was whether its success establishes voter-majority contact; the execution says it does not. In the retained run of the three-partition probe, the leader whose only reachable peer was the non-voter returned success in 0ms while its own latest configuration reported three voters, one non-voter and a quorum size of 2, and the leader was still in Leader state (parsed event index 1); the control partition that kept one voter reachable also returned success, which shows the harness does observe a genuine acknowledgement path (index 3); the control partition with no reachable peer did not return success at all, returning 'leadership lost while committing log' after 202ms with the node in Follower state, so the leader cannot reach the threshold on its own vote and the non-voter acknowledgement is what satisfied it in the first case (index 5). All three declared comparisons hold with the setup event matched as admission (correlations 1->0, 3->2, 5->4). The source explains the mechanism: verifyLeader asks every entry of leaderState.replState to acknowledge, startStopReplication creates such an entry for every configured server except the leader without consulting Suffrage, any successful AppendEntries or InstallSnapshot reply from such a peer calls notifyAll(true) and increments verifyFuture.votes, and the threshold compared against is quorumSize(), counted over voters alone. The same package treats voter eligibility strictly in its other leadership tests: checkLeaderLease does not count a non-voter, requestVote refuses a candidate that holds no vote, and quorumSize itself counts only voters, so the verify path is the outlier rather than a deliberate relaxation. \\\"\n   \\\"The consequence for reads stays bounded and is not what this receipt measures. The leader's lease is voter-only, and both Config.Validate and ReloadConfig enforce LeaderLeaseTimeout <= HeartbeatTimeout <= ElectionTimeout, so the old leader is normally removed before a voter majority elects a successor; the no-peer control is exactly that lease firing at 202ms with a 200ms lease. What the receipt does establish is the weaker but unconditional part: for an interval in which the leader exchanged nothing with any other voter, VerifyLeader reports success, so a caller relying on that call for read consistency is really relying on the lease timer rather than on the acknowledgements VerifyLeader collected.\\\"),\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"checkLeaderLease counts voters only, so a leader that has lost voter-majority contact steps down within about LeaderLeaseTimeout; the no-peer control shows this concretely (leadership lost at 202ms with a 200ms lease), which bounds the stale-read consequence rather than showing the verify decision support to be adequate.\\\",\n   \\\"Config.Validate keeps LeaderLeaseTimeout <= HeartbeatTimeout <= ElectionTimeout, and ReloadConfig re-runs ValidateConfig, so a leader cannot be configured to outlive a follower's election timer through the public reload API.\\\",\n   \\\"In the non-voter partition the other servers stayed in term 2 with no leader change, so the receipt does not witness a successor being elected while the old leader still verified; that half of the consequence remains unobserved.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The stale-read consequence still needs a successor elected while the old leader reports verify success, for example a leader-side stall or clock jump longer than ElectionTimeout - LeaderLeaseTimeout, or a verify request served before a ready lease case; the registered gap tracks that search and is not resolved by this receipt.\\\",\n   \\\"The probe uses one process with real Raft instances and in-memory transports, so it exercises the leader's own replication and verify paths but not process-level partitions or multi-host clocks; the partition was made by disconnecting transports in both directions.\\\",\n   \\\"One execution of each case is cited; repeatability of the timing-sensitive control (the 202ms lease step-down) is not established.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"b02d5ff23a504a8ea38116085ba8e23c\\\":[0,1,2,3,4,5]}\n },\n {\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@transfer_nonvoter\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"pick_server_voters\\\",\\\"follower_vote_grant\\\",\\\"docs_transfer\\\",\\\"start_stop_repl\\\"],\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"conditional\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"The documented purpose of LeadershipTransferToServer is to transition leadership to a specific server in the cluster, and the only target validation in the leader is a lookup in leaderState.replState, which holds an entry for every configured server except the leader regardless of Suffrage; a missing entry is the sole error. A non-voter therefore passes validation and is sent TimeoutNow, which makes it a Candidate with candidateFromLeadershipTransfer set, a flag that by design suppresses pre-vote so the node sends a real RequestVote with a higher term. Voters processing that request adopt the higher term and set themselves to Follower before the hasVote check rejects the candidate, so the candidate cannot collect a single grant, while the old leader loses leadership because it adopts the higher term too and its transfer goroutine then reports success from the leftLeaderLoop branch. The account is asserted on that source basis and stays conditional until the requested two-case probe reports what the call returns versus which server actually takes leadership; the controlling contrast is the same call naming a voter, and the note that auto-targeted LeadershipTransfer() skips non-voters via pickServer shows the library itself does not consider a non-voter a valid transfer target when it chooses.\\\"),\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The API does not state in its comment that the target must be a voter, and a caller who names only voters never reaches this path, so the defect depends on an accepted calling pattern rather than on the library's own choice of target.\\\",\n   \\\"LeadershipTransfer() without an explicit target filters non-voters in pickServer, which shows the intended transfer target set is the voter set and supports reading the targeted call as requiring the same premise.\\\",\n   \\\"A TimeoutNow that cannot be delivered (unreachable target) is reported as an error by the transfer path, so not every unusable target is silently accepted.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"No receipt exists yet for this question; the harness for the two-case probe is submitted with this update and its outcome is predicted, not observed.\\\",\n   \\\"Whether the cluster is briefly leaderless after the non-voter's campaign, and for how long, is registered as a gap: the current probe samples leadership state at the end of a 1500ms window, which is too coarse to bound a leaderless interval.\\\",\n   \\\"The claim concerns the reported result of the call and the requested target's inability to win; it does not assert data loss, since committed entries remain committed and a fresh election follows.\\\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@transfer_nonvoter\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"pick_server_voters\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Observe what LeadershipTransferToServer reports against which server actually takes leadership when the requested target is a non-voter, with the same call naming a voter as the only difference. Each case emits an assurance_transfer_target setup event describing the leader, the chosen target, its suffrage in the leader's latest configuration and the voter set, then an assurance_transfer_result event with the returned result, the target's and old leader's states, the leader set and terms after the call, and the time until any leader is observed.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n   \\\"Three voters plus one non-voter is a supported configuration; the non-voter is joined through the leader's own AddNonvoter call.\\\",\n   \\\"HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 200ms and CommitTimeout = 5ms satisfy Config.Validate; protocol version is the default (>= 3), so LeadershipTransferToServer is supported.\\\",\n   \\\"A voter target is a legal and expected use, so the voter case is the control that the probe can observe a real transfer rather than a probe that never succeeds.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\n   \\\"Bounding the length of any leaderless interval: leadership state is sampled at the end of the 1500ms observation window, so this probe does not measure an interval.\\\"\n  ]\n },\n \\\"prefix\\\":(\\\"Each case builds four real Raft instances in one process, each with its own InmemStore, InmemSnapshotStore and InmemTransport, fully connected before any node starts. Three voters are bootstrapped with BootstrapCluster from a configuration naming them as Voter; the fourth node is started without a configuration and joined through the elected leader's own AddNonvoter(id, address, 0, 5s) call, waiting until the leader's latest configuration reports it. \\\"\n  \\\"The target is then chosen by configuration role, never by a measured result: in the control case the first voter that is not the leader, in the probe case the joined non-voter; its suffrage is read back from the leader's latest configuration and reported in the setup event. The case calls leader.LeadershipTransferToServer(target.id, target.addr), waits up to 5s for the returned result, then waits up to 1500ms for the requested target to be observed as Leader and separately for any node to be Leader, and finally records the leader set, the maximum term across all four nodes and whether that term rose above the leader's term before the call. Both cases share the harness TestAssuranceLeadershipTransferTarget and are emitted under distinct case names.\\\"),\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_target\\\"}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"transfer_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"nil\\\"},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: what the call reported. Holds means the predicted success report was observed, which supports the defect account rather than contradicting it.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_became_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: the requested server never became leader within the observation window.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_became_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Voter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Voter target control: the same call does transfer leadership, so the non-voter outcome is not a probe that never transfers.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"transfer_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"nil\\\"},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Voter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Voter target control: the reported result for a transfer that does complete.\\\"}\n ]\n}\n\njson.dump(d, open('update.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nopen('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -6\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"2190c36cecef4055bdfd7441367c6e18\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 509.50018864299636, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": true, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"timeout_now\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"candidate_skips_prevote\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"vote_term_bump\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"transfer_target_lookup\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"transfer_lost_leadership\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"pick_server_voters\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"api_transfer_to_server\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"docs_transfer\"}, {\"object\": \"knowledge\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@transfer_accepts_nonvoter\"}, {\"object\": \"investigations\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@transfer_nonvoter\"}, {\"object\": \"interpretations\", \"action\": \"append\", \"target\": \"interpretations[0]\", \"investigation_id\": \"3b823834c8cb46da98e77d8e988bf5d9-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"source_ids\", \"executions\", \"conclusion\", \"rationale\", \"counterevidence\", \"limitations\"]}, {\"object\": \"interpretations\", \"action\": \"append\", \"target\": \"interpretations[1]\", \"investigation_id\": \"@transfer_nonvoter\"}, {\"object\": \"experiments\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"experiment\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Interpreted the completed probe receipt: all three comparisons hold, so the leader partitioned down to one reachable non-voter returned success in 0ms while its own configuration reported three voters and quorum size 2 (parsed result index 1), the voter-kept control also succeeded (index 3), and the no-peer control returned 'leadership lost while committing log' at 202ms with the node in Follower state (index 5) — establishing that the non-voter's acknowledgement satisfied the voter-sized quorum. The question account is now execution-backed ('explained'); the stale-read consequence remains conditional, with the lease-based counterevidence and the still-open gap about a legal successor-overlap condition. I also opened a second question on the authority-transition axis: LeadershipTransferToServer resolves its target through leaderState.replState (which holds non-voters), sends TimeoutNow, and the target's campaign forces voters to adopt a higher term and step down before the hasVote rejection, so the leader's transfer goroutine reports success for a transfer that cannot complete. A two-case probe (voter target as control, non-voter target) over the same named-event format is submitted with predictions recorded; its receipt, a gap about how long the cluster is leaderless, and refinement of the coarse leadership sampling remain unfinished.\"}"}}
